{
	"title": "Seuil : plus petit entier n tel que qⁿ dépasse une valeur (logarithme)",
	"description": "qⁿ < s ⟺ n > ln(s)/ln(q) en changeant le sens car ln(q) < 0 ; doublement d'un capital ; seuil d'une suite arithmético-géométrique (pièges : partie entière sans + 1, sens de l'inégalité)",
	"grades": ["T_SPE", "T_COMP"],
	"points": ["TCOMP-036", "TCOMP-037", "TSPE-174", "TSPE-175"],
	"theme": "Suites",
	"domain": "Seuils",
	"subdomain": "Logarithme",
	"level": 2,
	"status": "draft",
	"delay": 60,
	"variations": [
		{
			"statement": "Détermine le plus petit entier naturel $n$ tel que ${{eval:k/10;d}}^{n}<{{eval:10^(-t);d}}$.\n\n$n=?$",
			"variables": [
				{
					"name": "k",
					"expression": "5..9"
				},
				{
					"name": "t",
					"expression": "1..3"
				},
				{
					"name": "x",
					"expression": "eval:ln(10^(-t))/ln(k/10)"
				}
			],
			"conditions": ["abs(x-round(x)) > 0.001"],
			"blanks": [
				{
					"expectedAnswer": "{{eval:floor(x)+1}}"
				}
			],
			"correction": {
				"steps": [
					"La fonction $\\ln$ est strictement croissante sur $]0\\,;+\\infty[$ : ${{eval:k/10;d}}^{n}<{{eval:10^(-t);d}}\\iff n\\ln({{eval:k/10;d}})<\\ln({{eval:10^(-t);d}})$.",
					"$\\ln({{eval:k/10;d}})<0$ : en divisant, **on change le sens** : $n>\\dfrac{\\ln({{eval:10^(-t);d}})}{\\ln({{eval:k/10;d}})}\\approx{{eval:floor(x*100)/100;d}}$.",
					"Le plus petit entier qui convient est $n=\\textcolor{{{color:primary.0}}}{ {{eval:floor(x)+1}} }$."
				]
			}
		},
		{
			"statement": "Un capital de ${{c}}$ euros est placé à intérêts composés au taux annuel de ${{t}}\\,\\%$ : au bout de $n$ années, il vaut $C_n={{c}}\\times{{eval:1+t/100;d}}^{n}$.\n\nDétermine le plus petit entier naturel $n$ tel que le capital a doublé, c'est-à-dire $C_n\\geqslant{{eval:2*c}}$.\n\n$n=?$",
			"variables": [
				{
					"name": "c",
					"expression": "1000|2000|5000"
				},
				{
					"name": "t",
					"expression": "2..8"
				},
				{
					"name": "x",
					"expression": "eval:ln(2)/ln(1+t/100)"
				}
			],
			"conditions": ["abs(x-round(x)) > 0.001"],
			"blanks": [
				{
					"expectedAnswer": "{{eval:floor(x)+1}}"
				}
			],
			"correction": {
				"steps": [
					"$C_n\\geqslant{{eval:2*c}}\\iff{{eval:1+t/100;d}}^{n}\\geqslant2\\iff n\\ln({{eval:1+t/100;d}})\\geqslant\\ln 2$.",
					"$\\ln({{eval:1+t/100;d}})>0$ : $n\\geqslant\\dfrac{\\ln 2}{\\ln({{eval:1+t/100;d}})}\\approx{{eval:floor(x*100)/100;d}}$.",
					"Le plus petit entier qui convient est $n=\\textcolor{{{color:primary.0}}}{ {{eval:floor(x)+1}} }$."
				]
			}
		},
		{
			"statement": "Pour tout entier naturel $n$, $u_n={{eval:10*m}}-{{c}}\\times{{eval:k/10;d}}^{n}$.\n\nDétermine le plus petit entier naturel $n$ tel que $u_n>{{eval:10*m-1}}$.\n\n$n=?$",
			"variables": [
				{
					"name": "m",
					"expression": "2..9"
				},
				{
					"name": "c",
					"expression": "5..40"
				},
				{
					"name": "k",
					"expression": "5..9"
				},
				{
					"name": "x",
					"expression": "eval:-ln(c)/ln(k/10)"
				}
			],
			"conditions": ["abs(x-round(x)) > 0.001"],
			"blanks": [
				{
					"expectedAnswer": "{{eval:floor(x)+1}}"
				}
			],
			"correction": {
				"steps": [
					"$u_n>{{eval:10*m-1}}\\iff-{{c}}\\times{{eval:k/10;d}}^{n}>-1\\iff{{eval:k/10;d}}^{n}<\\dfrac{1}{ {{c}} }$.",
					"$\\ln$ est strictement croissante : $n\\ln({{eval:k/10;d}})<-\\ln {{c}}$ ; et $\\ln({{eval:k/10;d}})<0$, donc $n>\\dfrac{-\\ln {{c}}}{\\ln({{eval:k/10;d}})}\\approx{{eval:floor(x*100)/100;d}}$.",
					"Le plus petit entier qui convient est $n=\\textcolor{{{color:primary.0}}}{ {{eval:floor(x)+1}} }$."
				]
			}
		}
	],
